    "narrative": "The Austin Waves\u2019 offensive outlook for June 1st centers on high-upside matchups against mediocre arms, led by our premier outfield and utility assets. **Kyle Tucker** (74.54) and **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** (72.37) represent our strongest plays today. **Kyle Tucker** benefits from a soft matchup against Eduardo Rodriguez, where his elite profile is amplified by a favorable SP xERA of 4.53, while **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** leverages a strong platoon advantage against Sandy Alcantara. Despite a negative BvP flag, **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.** remains a primary start because his efficiency score is driven heavily by the dynamic platoon boost (+14%) and the opportunity to capitalize on Alcantara's high xERA. Meanwhile, **Andy Pages** (70.52) rounds out a productive trio, gaining significant momentum from the same advantageous matchup against Rodriguez.\n\nIn terms of strategy, we are leaning into speed and situational opportunities, though we must navigate a few marginal projections. **Nasim Nunez** (59.34) is a critical start today, not necessarily for his base hitting metrics, but because his 88% success rate against slow deliveries from Alcantara provides the necessary juice in the stolen base category, which remains our scarcest path to points. Conversely, **Miguel Vargas** (42.28) and **Sam Antonacci** (45.07) are operating near our floor due to a daunting matchup against Joe Ryan. While **Sam Antonacci** gets a slight nod due to a solid 0.372 xwOBA, both are playing strictly because they occupy key spots in the lineup. Our most difficult decision centered on **Josh Jung** (56.59); he narrowly missed the \"Strong\" tier but was cleared to start over potential bench options because of a neutral platoon and favorable SP skill data, providing a safer floor than waiting on volatility from reserves. \n\nFinally, please note that our depth is currently compromised by the scheduled off-days for **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.**, **Gunnar Henderson**, and **Jackson Merrill**, while **Luis Robert Jr.** remains locked in the IL slot. This unavailability forces us to ride the current lineup despite the risks associated with the \"Lineup Pending\" status for all starters. We are monitoring weather reports for the **Liam Hicks** and **Miguel Vargas** games, as any late-breaking precipitation could force a shuffle of our lower-tier starters to preserve our remaining game caps.",
